---
title: "Projects"
description: "Select the project each folder acts on and manage its resources and settings."
---

A project is the unit that owns your Photon resources — phone numbers, email
domains, API keys, webhooks, and billing. Every project belongs to an
[organization](/cli/organizations), which also holds its members.
`photon project` manages projects and everything inside them.

```sh
photon project list
photon project create --name "Support line" --slug support-line --link
photon project current
```

## Command overview

```text
photon link --project <project-id>
photon unlink
photon project
├── list [--search] [--created-after] [--created-before]
│          [--limit 30] [--page-token]
├── count [--search] [--created-after] [--created-before]
├── create --name <name> --slug <slug> [--link] [--idempotency-key <key>]
├── view
├── edit --name <name> [--idempotency-key <key>]
├── delete <project-id> [--yes]
├── current
├── agent-profile ...        # see Agent profile
├── api-key ...              # see API keys
├── billing ...              # see Billing
├── compliance ...           # see Call Registry
├── platform ...             # see Platform resources
├── telemetry ...            # see Developer telemetry
└── webhook ...              # see Webhooks
```

Every node generates its own help and shell completion. Run any of them with
`--help`, such as `photon project create --help`.

